  "source_derived_facts": [
    "Historical fitting uses one scalar measure per directed-region pair/condition/time/class pair, L1 liblinear logistic with C=1 and balanced row-class weights.",
    "The historical code performs global feature screening/imputation and its normalization can use transform-batch extrema; neither behavior is copied into the prospective fit boundaries.",
    "The original features are computed after known-category averaging. A label-independent observation table is a required new input whose authentic availability remains unverified.",
    "The inspected metadata CSV has284 rows; the required246-measure post-QC selection is not authenticated by taking its first246 rows.",
    "The246 retained domain incorporates full-cohort QC; conditioning on that historical domain does not establish fully nested feature eligibility."
  ],
  "prospective_differences": [
    "Training-only population standardization replaces author mixed-sigmoid preprocessing.",
    "Measure selection occurs inside explicit participant-disjoint inner folds; outer labels are absent from the fitting API.",
    "Primary selection/scoring may weight participants equally. This differs from historical mean-fold accuracy and does not change the source-style row-class weighting during fitting."
  ],
